      packages/apps/Sandbox             83d599f08df598770926afcccfd860f979418678

  Everything else is unchanged from 1vivy-rom.xml.

  DEFERRED - OSD caf-sm8850 DISPLAY SUBSTRATE. sm8850 builds display from the
  LineageOS common stack today: hardware/qcom-caf/sm8850/Android.bp is a linkfile
  to os_pickup_qssi.bp, which imports vendor/qcom/opensource/commonsys-intf/display
  and vendor/qcom/opensource/display. No manifest - crDroid, LineageOS, or any
  sibling sm8850 consumer - declares an sm8850 display project. Swapping in the
  OnePlus-SM8850-Development caf-sm8850 display stack is a build-integration
  change whose manifest projects, PRODUCT_SOONG_NAMESPACES entries and Android.bp
  pickup must land TOGETHER, so it is deliberately NOT done here; it belongs to
  the ltpo-adfr topic's integration commit. 1vivy/android_hardware_qcom_display
  and 1vivy/android_vendor_qcom_opensource_display-core are published on
  staging/features-v2/all but are intentionally UNCONSUMED by this manifest. The
  omission is deliberate, not an oversight.

  Only lineage_infiniti-bp4a-userdebug is built and runtime-validated upstream.
  macan, macanc and fairlady are present for source closure and static lunch
  resolution; no runtime result is implied for them.
